scope='''# C78 prior-art boundary and next research scope

Online estimation of nonlinear sensing around fixed or learned dynamics is established system identification. The primary [Recursive Identification of Systems with Noninvertible Output Nonlinearities](https://informatica.vu.lt/journal/INFORMATICA/article/573/info) describes recursive identification of linear and piecewise-linear nonlinear blocks. C78 is our ordinary bounded-history control, not a reproduction of that algorithm or a new method. Earlier Wiener-identification and compositional/continual world-model boundaries remain in C71/C76/C77.

Current primary-paper screening also checks the scope of claims before selecting another lead. [World Modeling through Spectral Alignment](https://arxiv.org/html/2610.15429v1), Sections4/5.3/5.4, explicitly relates temporal similarity to a behavioral-policy successor measure and states coverage assumptions excluding persistent clip attributes. Its temporal practical configuration omits target tempering/diagonal rescaling used in a stated invariance guarantee. Those are declared settings/assumptions, not an observed failure or a contradiction of the paper. No native SpecWM run or public-code availability audit is completed here. It blocks treating a generic statement about representation geometry, behavior-policy dependence or conditional invariance as an unexamined new idea.

The primary abstract of [Identification and Recovery of Linear Dynamics from Partial Trajectories](https://arxiv.org/html/2610.04455v1) already poses joint unknown transition/initial-state recovery from partial coordinate observations. Its full theorem/implementation was not audited here, and no result is reproduced. Do not relabel generic partial-observation state/dynamics recovery as novel based only on a different neural backbone.

Retire the normalized scalar sensor-calibration/composition premise as a lead after C75-C78's ordinary repairs. The general time-series-world-model objective remains intact and unachieved. Select the next candidate outside this repaired setup only after checking representative methods, actual code, task information and classical controls. The independent C71 original-budget three-seed/free-simulation assessment continues unchanged; no premature evaluation or new topology-OOD claim is made. No final research direction or new mechanism is accepted.
'''
